{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00597",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.5,
      "end_seconds": 13.45,
      "duration_seconds": 12.95,
      "text": "Doctor, there's a dark curtain coming down over my left eye, I noticed it this morning while I was doing the toast, and I nearly dropped the lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.68,
      "end_seconds": 29.3,
      "duration_seconds": 14.62,
      "text": "Okay, thank you for coming straight in. A dark curtain over the left eye, since this morning. Tell me more about how it looks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.04,
      "end_seconds": 42.97,
      "duration_seconds": 11.93,
      "text": "It starts at the top and drifts down, like a blind. My sister had a blind in her kitchen like that, always stuck halfway."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.48,
      "end_seconds": 50.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "Right. So from the top, going down. Is it still there now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.62,
      "end_seconds": 64.24,
      "duration_seconds": 12.62,
      "text": "It is, yes. About a third of the way over, I'd say. I can see around the edges, like looking through a keyhole."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.7,
      "end_seconds": 78.7,
      "duration_seconds": 12.0,
      "text": "Understood. I'm going to check a couple of things quickly, because this needs looking at properly today. Do you take any regular tablets?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.31,
      "end_seconds": 92.05,
      "duration_seconds": 11.74,
      "text": "I do, for my high blood pressure. Bisoprolol, maybe 5 mg? I'd have to check the box, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.73,
      "end_seconds": 104.04,
      "duration_seconds": 9.31,
      "text": "No worries. 5 mg, maybe, so we can confirm it later. How often do you take it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.99,
      "end_seconds": 118.75,
      "duration_seconds": 13.76,
      "text": "Every morning with my tea. Never miss it. Well, that's not strictly true, the odd morning I forget, usually when the grandchildren are here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.79,
      "end_seconds": 130.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.55,
      "text": "That's very common, so no judgement. Every morning, with a few missed. Now, let me take your pressure and pulse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.12,
      "end_seconds": 154.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "Go on. It'll be high, I've been in a state since breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.5,
      "end_seconds": 161.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "Your blood pressure is 158/94, and your pulse is 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.36,
      "end_seconds": 164.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Is that bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.82,
      "end_seconds": 187.85,
      "duration_seconds": 16.03,
      "text": "It's a bit up, which is not a surprise after this morning's fright. We'll come back to it. Now, I'll shine a light into your eyes. Look at the wall for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.4,
      "end_seconds": 198.93,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "I used to do this at the school, with the nurse, and the lights always made me sneeze."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.57,
      "end_seconds": 230.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "Just try not to sneeze for me. Both pupils are equal, and they react to light normally."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.11,
      "end_seconds": 234.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Grand. Is that good?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.49,
      "end_seconds": 250.87,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "That's reassuring. And the front of both eyes looks clear, nice and clean."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.12,
      "end_seconds": 262.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "I do wash them. My mother always said bathe the eyes in cold tea, can you believe it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.5,
      "end_seconds": 275.69,
      "duration_seconds": 12.19,
      "text": "Please don't, not with this. Tell me, apart from the eye, how has the rest of you been? Your general health?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.5,
      "end_seconds": 284.81,
      "duration_seconds": 8.31,
      "text": "Fine, really. Fit as a fiddle for my age, I walk the dog every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.99,
      "end_seconds": 299.56,
      "duration_seconds": 13.57,
      "text": "Good. Now, I want to be honest with you. I can't tell you from here what is causing this, and I'm not going to guess."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.33,
      "end_seconds": 305.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Ah. That sounds serious."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.01,
      "end_seconds": 321.67,
      "duration_seconds": 13.66,
      "text": "It needs a specialist with the right equipment, and soon. A sudden curtain like yours is something we send to the eye hospital the same day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.15,
      "end_seconds": 328.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Today? I've the dog in the car."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.36,
      "end_seconds": 340.09,
      "duration_seconds": 10.73,
      "text": "Today, yes. I'll write a letter and send you straight to the eye casualty at the hospital. Can someone drive you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.4,
      "end_seconds": 351.34,
      "duration_seconds": 8.94,
      "text": "My neighbour's outside, he gave me the lift. Thomas, a lovely man, he does the bins as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.08,
      "end_seconds": 359.48,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Perfect. Please don't drive yourself, and don't wait until later this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.61,
      "end_seconds": 363.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Right. And the dog?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.74,
      "end_seconds": 377.03,
      "duration_seconds": 12.29,
      "text": "Thomas can take the dog home first, if he's quick. But you go on to the hospital straight after that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.66,
      "end_seconds": 385.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "I will. Honestly, I thought it'd be a drop of something and home for lunch."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.69,
      "end_seconds": 405.04,
      "duration_seconds": 16.35,
      "text": "I know. So, just to repeat it: the left eye, a dark curtain since this morning, and you're going to the eye hospital today with my letter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 406.35,
      "end_seconds": 410.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Eye hospital, today, with the letter. Got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.22,
      "end_seconds": 419.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "Good. They'll take over from here. Mind yourself, and tell them everything you've told me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 420.91,
      "end_seconds": 424.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "I will. Thanks, doctor. God bless."
    }
  ]
}
